# Line endings for files that are executed by Linux inside a container.
#
# This checkout has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites tracked text files to
# CRLF in the working tree. That is harmless for anything Windows runs, and not
# harmless for anything the container runs:
#
#   - docker/Dockerfile uses a `RUN <<EOF` heredoc. BuildKit writes the body to
#     a file and hands it to the shell; with CRLF every line ends in a literal
#     carriage return, so `set -xe` becomes `set -xe$'\r'` — an invalid option.
#   - docker/dev-entrypoint.sh is bind-mounted and executed directly. A CRLF
#     shebang fails with the classic `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`.
#
# Both failures are obscure enough to cost an hour, so they are pinned here
# rather than left to whoever clones next.

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
